<section class="cp-section" id="landscape">
  <h2 class="cp-section-title">Forex Trading Landscape in Pakistan</h2>
  <p class="cp-lead">Forex trading attracts Pakistani traders seeking access to global currency markets. However, local rules and international broker regulations differ. Traders should understand the legal and funding risks before opening accounts.</p>
  <p>The Securities and Exchange Commission of Pakistan (SECP) regulates Pakistan's securities market. Traders should not assume an offshore forex broker has local authorisation. The State Bank of Pakistan (SBP) also regulates foreign exchange transactions. Check official notices and applicable rules before sending money abroad.</p>
  <p>International brokers may operate under regulators such as the FCA or ASIC. Their protections depend on the broker's legal entity and account registration. Check the regulator's official register and the broker's licence details. Also review withdrawal rules, payment restrictions, and client fund protections.</p>
  <div class="cp-insight"><p><strong>Important:</strong> Broker availability does not confirm local authorisation or lawful funding. Verify current rules through official Pakistani sources before depositing funds.</p></div>
</section>

